# UPSTREAM.sha256 - reproducible fingerprint for ulfjack/ryu
# at commit 4c0618b0e44f7ef027ebae05d2cc7812048f7c8f.
#
# 38 records, one `<hex>  <path>` line each, in `sha256sum` format, grouped
# by what each path is for. Check them from the repository root with:
#
#     sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256
#
# Every path named here is shipped in `build.zig.zon` `.paths`, so the same
# command also works in an unpacked package fetched by a dependent.
#
# How the original digests were produced, 2026-10-01: each file was read as raw bytes
# and hashed with SHA-256 through Bun (`Bun.file(path).arrayBuffer()` and
# `new Bun.CryptoHasher("sha256")`). No shell hashing or git command produced
# those original lines. The 38 paths now total 2689946 bytes.
# The previous 2689837-byte total and all 38 digests were re-hashed on 2026-10-02 and
# matched unchanged; the 2688626-byte figure this header carried until then was
# stale.
# The later translate.h include-citation correction adds 50 bytes and changes
# only Group F's digest. The unchanged comparison above predates that edit.
# The prominent change notice on the existing ryu/ryu.h:24 adds 59 bytes;
# Group B's digest was re-derived with sha256sum on 2026-10-02. No line shifted.
#
# What this record is: a hash of THIS WORKING TREE.
# What it is not: a Git object id, a signature, or a re-derivation from the
# pinned commit. That the working tree differs from commit
# 4c0618b0e44f7ef027ebae05d2cc7812048f7c8f in exactly the two paths this file
# names, `.gitignore` and `ryu/ryu.h`, is established elsewhere, by the
# pinned-commit diff in `.github/workflows/verify.yml` and by the archive
# receipt in `UPSTREAM.md`. The two are complementary: this record fails if
# any hashed byte moves here, whatever a commit says; the diff fails if any
# other upstream-tracked path differs from the commit, whatever this record
# says.
#
# One upstream-tracked file in this record is edited, and the record discloses
# it rather than claiming a pristine tree. `ryu/ryu.h:24` reads
# `#include <stdint.h>` here and `#include <inttypes.h>` at commit
# 4c0618b0e44f7ef027ebae05d2cc7812048f7c8f.
# That include carries one name into the header, `uint32_t`, used in the six
# `precision` parameters at `ryu/ryu.h:34-40`, and no `PRI*` or `SCN*` macro;
# `uint32_t` is declared by `<stdint.h>` (C99 7.18.1), which is the header
# `<inttypes.h>` includes to reach the same type. The reason is portability,
# not preference: NetBSD's `<inttypes.h>` closes its declarations with
# `__END_DECLS`, whose replacement list starts with a `_Pragma` the pinned
# translator reads as ordinary tokens. Nine cells of the platform matrix are
# NetBSD cells, and all nine reach this header through it.
#
# The deviation is exactly that line. Upstream's bytes for this path are 1360
# bytes hashing to b7feab0ba1df5e9ef3d602f386592ad152491405e49b408fb21c0e0e9e6bfb16;
# replacing that one include with `<stdint.h>` and its inline change notice
# reproduces this tree's 1417 bytes exactly; no other native path differs.
# No declaration, type, signature, constant or algorithm changes.
# Three of the five compiled translation units include the header this record
# measures (`d2s.c`, `f2s.c`, `d2fixed.c`); the two parsers include
# `<stdint.h>` of their own and `ryu/ryu_parse.h`, and `generic_128.c`, which
# only `-Dgeneric128` compiles, includes `ryu/ryu_generic_128.h`. Neither of
# those headers is patched. Group B therefore carries the patched digest, with
# upstream's kept beside it. `translate.h` states the same deviation in prose,
# and `.github/workflows/verify.yml` enforces it: it hashes upstream's blob at
# the pinned commit and this tree's file, puts the one include back, and
# requires upstream's digest. A `git diff --exit-code` against the pinned
# commit over `ryu/` reports this one path, by design.
#
# Excluded, deliberately, with the reason in each case:
#   * `.gitignore` - an upstream-tracked file this fork edits, additively, so
#     its bytes are the fork's rather than upstream's. It is the only edited
#     path left out of the records; the other edited path, `ryu/ryu.h`, is
#     hashed at its patched digest, as the section above says.
#   * `third_party/` - separate upstream corpora (gtest, junit, mersenne,
#     jaffer, double-conversion, mersenne_java) that carry their own licences
#     and that nothing in this package compiles or links. See `NOTICE.md`.
#   * the remaining upstream-tracked paths (`src/`, `scripts/`, `lean/`,
#     `ryu/benchmark/`, `ryu/Makefile`, `ryu/BUILD`, `CMakeLists.txt`,
#     `MODULE.bazel`, the benchmark scripts, `.bazelrc`, `.bazelversion`,
#     `.classpath`, `lakefile.toml`, `lake-manifest.json`,
#     `lean-toolchain`, `.github/workflows/presubmit.yml`) - carried whole,
#     compiled by nothing here, and covered by the pinned-commit diff.
#   * everything this fork wrote, except `translate.h`: `build.zig`,
#     `build.zig.zon`, `zig/root.zig`, `tests.zig`, `smoke.zig`, `consumer/`,
#     `.github/workflows/verify.yml` and the fork's own documentation. Those
#     are expected to change.
#   * `zig-out/` and `.zig-cache/` - build output, absent from `.paths` and
#     ignored by `.gitignore`.
#   * this record itself.

